  "title": "Weekly Observation, October 3rd — NVIDIA's Solar Throne, Unshaken",
  "summary": "With NVIDIA holding the Throne at $5.68T, the surges of SpaceX and TSMC signal a shift in cosmic order.",
  "body": "<h3>Securing the Solar Position</h3><p>NVIDIA claimed the center of the universe this week with a market cap of $5.68T. Following last week's Throne, it continues to hold the solar position, demonstrating how robust the AI-driven new order has become. Apple ($4.84T), Alphabet ($4.15T), and Microsoft ($3.83T) remain giant planets, but the distance from NVIDIA shows no signs of narrowing.</p><h3>Movement in the Heat</h3><p>Looking at the top 3 weekly gainers, the advances of SpaceX (+5.8%) and TSMC (+5.0%) stand out. These are signals detecting a seismic shift in semiconductors and space industries. NVIDIA also continued its upward trend with +4.5% for the week, reflecting positive momentum across the entire sector. Meanwhile, the financial and consumer segments showed weekly weakness. The declines of JPMorgan Chase (-3.5%), Walmart (-3.4%), and Eli Lilly (-3.1%) make this clear.</p><h3>Shifts in the Universe's Gateway</h3><p>As ASML entered the observation range, attention to the semiconductor production equipment sector heightened. Conversely, Visa was removed from the observation list, suggesting that the cosmic order continues to be reorganized.</p><h3>Observing Latent Forces</h3><p>Though not yet ranking in the top positions, there are companies worth noting by momentum index. The upward momentum of Sandisk (321), KIOXIA Holdings (283), and Dell (276) carries the potential to reshape the cosmic landscape ahead. These movements in memory semiconductors and IT infrastructure sectors serve as clues to reading which direction the universe is rotating.</p><p>The universe turns, and records remain. Whether this week's observation foreshadows tomorrow's order will be proven by next week's observation.</p><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#9c7a3a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#f2ba3c\"/></linearG